    "body": "## Summary\n\nRecords the CI failure discovered after ADR-034's implementation as a **Post-Implementation Note** in ADR-034. **Ninth correction pattern in the arc's record** — and the first about verification methodology itself, not a feature-level prediction error.\n\n## The finding\n\nCI has been failing on `main` since ADR-034's implementation merged (#179):\n\n| PR | Branch | Build & Test |\n|---|---|---|\n| #177 (docs) | `docs/adr-034-img-absolute` | ✅ 6m53s |\n| #178 (docs) | `docs/adr-034-svg-amendment` | ✅ 1m59s |\n| **#179 (impl)** | `feat/img-absolute` | ❌ 36s (librsvg added here) |\n| #180 (docs) | `docs/adr-034-implemented` | ❌ 41s (inherits) |\n| **#181 (url fix)** | `fix/protocol-relative-url` | ❌ 39s (still failing) |\n| #182 (CI fix) | `fix/ci-librsvg-dependency` | ✅ 1m17s (fix works) |\n\nRoot cause: ADR-034 added `pkg_check_modules(RSVG REQUIRED librsvg-2.0)` to `CMakeLists.txt:57`, but `.github/workflows/build.yml` was never updated to install `librsvg2-dev`.\n\n```\n-- Checking for module 'librsvg-2.0'\n--   Package 'librsvg-2.0' not found\nCMake Error: The following required packages were not found:\n  - librsvg-2.0\n  CMakeLists.txt:57 (pkg_check_modules)\n```\n\n## The discipline gap, honestly\n\nThe session's \"merged cleanly\" signal throughout the ADR-034 cycle was **local-only**. Local builds pass 421→425 cases / 1737→1741 assertions. `gh run list` was never checked after any merge.\n\nLocal `pkg-config --exists librsvg-2.0` succeeds (developer machine has `librsvg2-dev`). CI doesn't (workflow install step is missing it).\n\n**This is the exact pattern ADR-028 identified** — \"a subsystem's local tests can pass while the subsystem is never reached in production\" — applied to CI itself. Local tests pass; the *CI runner* never reaches them because configure fails first.\n\nWorse than ADR-028's URL bug: that one was caught by feature measurement within one cycle. This was caught by the user noticing a red badge at 342 workflow runs, four merges deep.\n\n## The fix (already merged as #182)\n\n1. Add `librsvg2-dev` to the workflow's `apt-get install`\n2. Expand \"Verify GTK 4 bindings\" to verify all five pkg-config modules; rename to \"Verify CMake pkg-config dependencies\"\n\nThe verify step now **encodes the lesson structurally** — future missing-dependency breakage fails at a named CI step, not a red badge buried in a configure log.\n\n## Why ninth correction pattern\n\nPrior eight corrections (025/026/027 URL-bug post-fixes, 028 grid misdiagnosis, 029 three corrections, 030 actuals-exceed, 031 misreading, 032 negative result, 033 byte-identical validation) were all **feature-level**.\n\n**This is the first about verification methodology itself.** The session's \"measure before, measure after, preserve corrections\" discipline is necessary but not sufficient — it also needs \"check every automated signal that claims success, not just local ones.\"\n\n## What this means for future ADRs\n\n- Every merge followed by `gh run list --limit 1` to confirm CI green before next block\n- Workflow's verify step now covers every CMake pkg-config module — future ADRs adding a new dependency must extend it (visible in the file, hard to forget)\n- Local + CI are both signals; local-only was the gap\n\n## What changed\n\n- `docs/decisions/034-img-absolute.md` — Post-Implementation Note added at end of Implementation section\n\n## What didn't change\n\n- Zero code changes\n- Test count: 425 / 1741 (unchanged by this docs PR)\n- Full suite green\n- CI green on main after #182 merged\n\nRefs #179 #180 #181 #182\n",
